    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty heavy way to look at it. but if walking out is the only \"honest\" move, then why do people fight so hard to stay? why is there this massive social pressure to just keep grinding through the exhaustion even when it feels fundamentally broken? is it just fear of the unknown, or is there actually some logical reason to keep staying in the loop?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
